{
  "note": "Hand-written (phase 5 design 5.3; PRD main 424-431, 441-442). Supplies a note suggests, and what a bundle applies: suggestSupplies and bundleLines in packages/presets/src/supplies.ts and apps/mobile/lib/presets/ (P2-supplies). The readers are packages/presets/test/supplies.test.ts and the phone's supplies test. Phase 6 calls them; this phase pins them. suggestSupplies({maps, items, noteTypeKey, definition, answers}): maps are the team's active field supply maps, each {id, body}; items the team's items by id, each {state}; noteTypeKey the note's type and definition its own version (one of this file's `definitions`, which pass forms' validate()); answers what the suggesting person may see of the note (visibleAnswers, forms 7.1), so an answer hidden from them, or in a field hidden by a condition, is not there to fire anything. A map fires only on a note of its noteTypeKey. With no path it fires once for the note, whatever the answers. Otherwise it fires where the note holds an answer at its path (its entry part put back: once for each entry of a repeating section that holds one, each wound its own firing) and the answer passes its when: answered, any answer; includes c, a choose-many holding c or a choose-one that is c; equals v, a choose-one that is v, a choose-many holding v alone, a number equal to v, a tick when v is true. A path this version of the note type lacks never fires. Each firing adds each line's quantity: qty, or {fromPath}, the answer at that path in the same entry (or row), read as a whole number from 0 to 99; anything else, or no answer, gives 0. A line whose item is archived, or not among items, is skipped. The answer is [{itemId, qty, mapId}]: one suggestion per map and item, the quantities of that map's lines naming that item summed over every firing; one that sums to 0 is left out. Two maps naming one item give a suggestion each. Suggestions are in the order of the maps given, each map's items in the order its lines first name them. bundleLines(bundle, items, multiplier): each line of the bundle body in order, {itemId, qty: the line's qty times multiplier, checked: the line's core}, a line whose item is archived or not among items left out. multiplier is the number of times the bundle is given (\"- 2 kits +\"), a whole number from 1. Ids and names are made up.",
